("p", "**Idea of the proof.** Let the tangent XY touch the circle with centre O at P, and take any other point Q on XY. Q lies outside the circle, so OQ is longer than the radius OP. Thus OP is the **shortest distance** from O to the line XY, and the shortest distance is the perpendicular. Hence OP is perpendicular to XY."),
