("p", "**Proof.** Let PA and PB be tangents from P to a circle with centre O. In right triangles OAP and OBP: OA = OB (radii), OP is common, angle OAP = angle OBP = 90&deg;. So the triangles are congruent (RHS), and **PA = PB**. It also follows that angle APO = angle BPO, so **OP bisects the angle between the tangents**, and angle OPA = angle OPB."),
